        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maeve, Queen Mab, William Shakespeare\n- Concepts: Irish and English legend, fairies, pronunciation\n- Works: Romeo and Juliet\n\nFacts:\n- Maeve is associated with the fairy queen Queen Mab in Irish and English legend.\n- Queen Mab is pronounced \"M/ă/v.\"\n- William Shakespeare's play Romeo and Juliet refers to Queen Mab as a fairy.\n- In Romeo and Juliet, Queen Mab is described as \"the fairies' midwife.\"",
